WEBVTT

00:00.796 --> 00:02.196
♪ Men. ♪

00:08.665 --> 00:10.232
Yeah, I gotta tell ya,

00:10.233 --> 00:12.334
my brother does basically
the same thing

00:12.335 --> 00:14.336
in the shower every day

00:14.337 --> 00:20.075
and he has absolutely
no muscle tone in his arms.

00:20.076 --> 00:22.177
All right, I'm out of here.
Hold on a sec.

00:22.178 --> 00:24.363
What does this look
like to you, Berta?

00:24.364 --> 00:26.382
Your brother in the shower?

00:28.034 --> 00:30.452
You hear that?
It's not just me.

00:31.721 --> 00:34.790
Thanks, Berta.
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:34.791 --> 00:36.625
No, you won't.

00:36.626 --> 00:40.529
I told you, I'm going to a
family reunion for a few days.

00:40.530 --> 00:43.432
But what about me?

00:43.433 --> 00:45.867
All right,

00:45.868 --> 00:48.370
let's go through this
one more time.

00:52.208 --> 00:56.412
I arranged to have a friend
fill in for me.

00:56.413 --> 00:58.580
Her name is Esmerelda.

00:58.581 --> 00:59.898
I have given her

00:59.899 --> 01:01.617
detailed instructions

01:01.618 --> 01:03.552
about how you like things done
around here.

01:03.553 --> 01:06.105
Did you tell her to roll me over
on my stomach

01:06.106 --> 01:09.658
so I don't choke
on my own vomit?

01:09.659 --> 01:12.094
That's number one on the list.

01:12.095 --> 01:14.263
Is she hot?

01:14.264 --> 01:15.898
She was in the '70s.

01:15.899 --> 01:18.033
I guess it's better that way.

01:18.034 --> 01:21.036
Yeah, it's tough enough that
you and I have sexual tension.

01:22.972 --> 01:26.809
Oh, by the way, you
promised me vacation pay.

01:26.810 --> 01:29.378
Okay.

01:29.379 --> 01:32.131
How much did
we agree on?

01:32.132 --> 01:34.216
That looks about right.

01:34.217 --> 01:36.685
Bye.

01:36.686 --> 01:38.854
See you tomorrow.

01:42.992 --> 01:45.427
Uncle Charlie in there?

01:45.428 --> 01:46.495
Yep.

01:46.496 --> 01:47.763
Drunk?

01:47.764 --> 01:49.031
Hammered.

01:49.032 --> 01:50.332
You clean him out?

01:50.333 --> 01:53.285
Would I do that
to my little buddy?

01:53.286 --> 01:54.903
Thank you, Berta.

01:55.839 --> 01:58.273
All right, have a good
weekend, Uncle Charlie.

01:58.274 --> 02:01.176
Enjoy your family reunion.

02:01.177 --> 02:02.144
What?

02:02.145 --> 02:03.879
What?

02:03.880 --> 02:04.913
You know, you still owe me

02:04.914 --> 02:06.248
for that pizza
from the other night.

02:06.249 --> 02:10.085
Oh, yeah, sorry.

02:10.086 --> 02:11.420
How much was it?

02:11.421 --> 02:12.654
That'll do it.

02:12.655 --> 02:15.290
Jake, let's go.
Your mom's outside.

02:15.291 --> 02:16.958
See ya,
Uncle Charlie.

02:16.959 --> 02:18.761
See ya, buddy.

02:18.762 --> 02:21.296
Thanks for the pizza.

02:21.297 --> 02:22.765
When did you guys have pizza?

02:22.766 --> 02:24.800
I have no idea.

02:27.504 --> 02:31.073
Hey, Charlie,
you remember Lyndsey?

02:31.074 --> 02:32.875
Nope.

02:35.779 --> 02:37.980
Hey, look.

02:37.981 --> 02:39.498
(chuckles)

02:44.120 --> 02:46.205
I'm exercising.

02:47.423 --> 02:50.425
Oh, maybe you ought
to sit down for a minute.

02:50.426 --> 02:52.361
Good idea.

02:52.362 --> 02:54.763
I'm getting
a little dizzy.

02:54.764 --> 02:56.965
I hope I don't have
a heart problem.

02:56.966 --> 02:59.968
No, you have
a drinking problem.

02:59.969 --> 03:01.670
That's a relief.

03:01.671 --> 03:03.872
So who's this Lyndsey?

03:03.873 --> 03:08.577
You remember-- Lyndsey,
early 40s, blonde, pretty.

03:08.578 --> 03:10.679
No recollection.

03:10.680 --> 03:12.314
I burned her house down.

03:12.315 --> 03:14.583
She left me, went back
to her ex-husband?

03:14.584 --> 03:16.852
Keep going.

03:16.853 --> 03:20.322
Nice, full, very natural
looking C-cup?

03:20.323 --> 03:22.574
Oh, right, Lyndsey.

03:22.575 --> 03:24.526
Here we go.

03:33.469 --> 03:34.937
What are you doing?

03:34.938 --> 03:36.238
Child-proofing you.

03:36.239 --> 03:37.806
Thank you.

03:37.807 --> 03:40.209
So you're-you're dating

03:40.210 --> 03:42.077
Lindsay Lohan?

03:42.078 --> 03:44.980
No, no, Lyndsey MacElroy.

03:44.981 --> 03:46.398
Anyway, she called
and apparently

03:46.399 --> 03:48.267
things aren't working out
with the ex-husband,

03:48.268 --> 03:49.935
and even though she
didn't exactly say she

03:49.936 --> 03:52.688
wanted to get back together, I
am going to meet her for dinner.

03:52.689 --> 03:53.956
Well, that's great.
Mm-hmm.

03:53.957 --> 03:55.190
Good for you.

03:55.825 --> 03:57.893
How do I look?

03:57.894 --> 04:01.864
Like Lance Armstrong
after a three-day drunk.

04:01.865 --> 04:03.699
Nice.

04:03.700 --> 04:05.000
Mm-hmm.

04:05.668 --> 04:09.204
You are a good brother, Alan.

04:09.205 --> 04:11.273
Have some money.

04:11.274 --> 04:13.342
Thanks.

04:13.343 --> 04:15.427
If I were really
a good brother,

04:15.428 --> 04:17.279
I would stage
an intervention.

04:17.280 --> 04:19.631
Thanks for the pizza.

04:32.996 --> 04:35.764
Eureka.

04:35.765 --> 04:38.367
I've invented
the drinking helmet.

04:39.067 --> 04:42.167
== Sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00ff00">elderman&lt;/font> ==
== for &lt;font color=00FFFF>www.addic7ed.com&lt;/font> ==

04:42.272 --> 04:44.806
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

04:44.807 --> 04:46.626
♪ Ah. ♪
♪ Men. ♪
♪ Men. ♪

04:46.726 --> 04:49.826
&lt;font color="#00ff00">♪ Two and a Half Men 8x09 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00ffff">A Good Time in Central Africa&lt;/font>
&lt;font color=#FFFF00>Original Air Date on November 15, 2010&lt;/font>

04:49.916 --> 04:51.951
♪ Men. ♪

04:55.222 --> 04:57.039
(sighs)

05:02.062 --> 05:03.512
Hello?

05:04.347 --> 05:06.549
(speaking Spanish)

05:12.055 --> 05:16.692
Oh, man, did I go
to Tijuana last night?

05:20.564 --> 05:23.449
Me... you...

05:23.450 --> 05:26.018
Not married, are we?

05:30.824 --> 05:32.625
I guess if the answer was yes,

05:32.626 --> 05:35.027
she wouldn't be polishing
the piano.

05:38.748 --> 05:41.200
Hey, Alan, quick question.

05:41.201 --> 05:42.701
Yeah?

05:42.702 --> 05:45.704
Who is that in
our living room?

05:45.705 --> 05:46.872
That's Esmerelda.

05:46.873 --> 05:48.908
Gonna need more.

05:48.909 --> 05:50.509
Berta's friend?

05:50.510 --> 05:51.510
Keep going.

05:51.511 --> 05:53.378
Berta went
to her family reunion.

05:53.379 --> 05:54.880
Esmerelda's filling in for her.

05:54.881 --> 05:59.551
Oh. It would have been nice
if she'd given me a heads-up.

05:59.552 --> 06:03.055
Aren't you going to ask me
about last night?

06:03.056 --> 06:04.773
Oh, yeah.

06:04.774 --> 06:08.277
What did I do last night?

06:08.278 --> 06:12.198
Somehow I spent
almost all my money.

06:12.199 --> 06:14.633
No, I meant
what I did last night.

06:14.634 --> 06:17.102
Oh. No.

06:17.103 --> 06:19.755
Lyndsey wants
to get back together.

06:20.707 --> 06:21.740
C-cups.

06:21.741 --> 06:23.976
Right. Lyndsey.

06:23.977 --> 06:26.245
She did split up
with her ex-husband Chris.

06:26.246 --> 06:28.597
Said she realized
she didn't want to go backwards.

06:28.598 --> 06:32.585
In what universe is dating you
not going backwards?

06:32.586 --> 06:35.921
I know. This guy must be
some kind of mess.

06:37.657 --> 06:40.025
Breakfast, Señor Harper?

06:40.026 --> 06:41.477
Why is she saying breakfast?

06:41.478 --> 06:43.262
Am I supposed to make her
breakfast?

06:43.263 --> 06:45.614
She'll make it for you.

06:45.615 --> 06:48.784
Try the huevos rancheros--
they're amazing.

06:48.785 --> 06:51.003
(speaking Spanish)

06:55.575 --> 06:57.042
&lt;i>Muy bien.&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Gracias.&lt;/i>

06:57.043 --> 07:00.212
Where did you learn
to speak Spanish?

07:00.213 --> 07:02.665
Junior high, high school,
college,

07:02.666 --> 07:05.918
two years of chiropractic school
in Mexico.

07:05.919 --> 07:08.320
You say that like
I'm supposed to know.

07:08.321 --> 07:11.090
You are supposed to know.
You're my brother.

07:33.280 --> 07:36.615
(Esmerelda laughing)

07:36.616 --> 07:37.649
What's so funny?

07:37.650 --> 07:39.451
Are you talking about me?

07:39.452 --> 07:41.387
She says she likes your hat.

07:44.090 --> 07:46.342
♪ Men. ♪

07:47.344 --> 07:50.045
CHARLIE:
Alan! Come here, quick!

07:50.046 --> 07:53.899
Please God,
don't let it be a dead girl.

07:57.570 --> 07:59.238
What is it?

07:59.239 --> 08:01.640
Open my door and
tell me what you see.

08:01.641 --> 08:04.076
Why? What do &lt;i>you&lt;/i> see?

08:04.878 --> 08:06.779
Just look.

08:06.780 --> 08:08.731
Are the flying monkeys back?

08:08.732 --> 08:10.883
Don't joke about that, Alan.

08:11.718 --> 08:13.736
Wow.

08:13.737 --> 08:15.054
Esmerelda did this?

08:15.055 --> 08:16.355
Can you believe it?

08:16.356 --> 08:17.656
The fresh cut flowers,

08:17.657 --> 08:18.958
the carafe of lemon water.

08:18.959 --> 08:20.709
She even laid out
my robe and slippers.

08:20.710 --> 08:21.961
Since when
do you have slippers?

08:21.962 --> 08:24.296
I don't know. Is it
possible she made them?

08:26.366 --> 08:28.734
She put a chocolate on your pillow?
Yup.

08:28.735 --> 08:30.636
See what it says?

08:30.637 --> 08:32.037
&lt;i>"Felicidad."&lt;/i>

08:32.038 --> 08:33.472
That means
"Merry Christmas," right?

08:33.473 --> 08:35.407
It means "happiness."

08:35.408 --> 08:38.510
You sure? What about that song,
uh, "Felicidad Navidas"?

08:38.511 --> 08:40.612
&lt;i>"Feliz Navidad"?&lt;/i>

08:40.613 --> 08:42.547
Tomato, tamale.

08:42.548 --> 08:43.849
The point is,

08:43.850 --> 08:46.151
Esmerelda is
a terrific housekeeper.

08:46.152 --> 08:47.920
I didn't get
a chocolate.

08:47.921 --> 08:49.355
You're not Señor Harper.

08:49.356 --> 08:50.823
I'm &lt;i>a&lt;/i> Señor Harper.

08:50.824 --> 08:53.359
Yes, but not the Señor Harper
that pays her.

08:54.577 --> 08:56.695
Come on, you got
to see this.

08:56.696 --> 08:58.831
She still could have
given me a chocolate.

08:58.832 --> 09:00.933
How much could it cost?

09:00.934 --> 09:02.668
Look!

09:02.669 --> 09:03.869
That's not a swan.

09:03.870 --> 09:05.938
That's my towel.

09:05.939 --> 09:07.172
Nice touch.

09:07.173 --> 09:08.507
Had me fooled
at first.

09:08.508 --> 09:10.676
I tried to kill it.

09:11.711 --> 09:13.178
And look.

09:13.179 --> 09:15.681
She folded my toilet paper
into a little point.

09:15.682 --> 09:17.750
After breakfast,
I used some, stood up, shaved,

09:17.751 --> 09:20.586
and when I looked back,
I swear it was pointed again.

09:20.587 --> 09:22.421
Is that a votive candle?

09:22.422 --> 09:23.689
Yup.

09:23.690 --> 09:25.791
She's praying that I have
pleasant bowel movements.

09:25.792 --> 09:27.192
Oh, please.

09:27.193 --> 09:28.360
No, no, no, it's working.

09:28.361 --> 09:31.663
This morning, soft, firm,
easy peasy.

09:31.664 --> 09:33.432
But wait, there's more.

09:33.433 --> 09:35.067
Come on.

09:36.953 --> 09:39.455
Tada!

09:39.456 --> 09:41.373
She bought you a new grill?!

09:41.374 --> 09:42.975
No, no, no, this
is the old grill.

09:42.976 --> 09:44.109
You know what she did?

09:44.110 --> 09:46.278
What?
She cleaned it.

09:46.279 --> 09:48.147
She cleaned the grill?

09:48.148 --> 09:49.681
Berta never cleans the grill.

09:49.682 --> 09:50.883
Tell me about it.

09:50.884 --> 09:53.152
She only comes out on the deck
to smoke pot.

09:53.153 --> 09:54.019
Señor Harper?

09:54.020 --> 09:55.187
Yes?

09:55.188 --> 09:57.756
She's talking to me,
Baba Looey. Yes?

09:58.825 --> 10:00.592
Hell, yeah, &lt;i>botanas.&lt;/i>

10:06.633 --> 10:08.500
What's that mean,
"screw you"?

10:08.501 --> 10:09.968
Basically.

10:09.969 --> 10:11.970
I love this woman.

10:11.971 --> 10:13.355
Esmerelda, &lt;i>te amo.&lt;/i>

10:13.356 --> 10:15.074
&lt;i>Ay, Señor.&lt;/i>

10:15.075 --> 10:16.475
I thought you didn't
speak Spanish.

10:16.476 --> 10:18.977
I don't, but I do know
how to say "I love you"

10:18.978 --> 10:20.512
and "How much for
a happy ending?"

10:20.513 --> 10:21.747
in, like, 17
different languages.

10:21.748 --> 10:23.198
You're kidding.

10:23.199 --> 10:26.385
(speaking foreign
language and clicking)

10:26.386 --> 10:30.589
In case you ever want to have
a good time in Central Africa.

10:33.760 --> 10:35.660
♪ Men. ♪

10:35.661 --> 10:37.229
(doorbell ringing)

10:37.230 --> 10:38.297
CHARLIE:
Alan, get that!

10:38.298 --> 10:40.265
Esmerelda's giving
me a pedicure!

10:40.266 --> 10:43.502
Pedicure. I can't even get
a freakin' chocolate.

10:45.522 --> 10:46.872
Hello, Alan.

10:46.873 --> 10:49.041
Chris! Hey.

10:49.042 --> 10:50.642
Uh, what brings you by?

10:50.643 --> 10:52.544
Well, Lyndsey mentioned
that you two are dating again,

10:52.545 --> 10:53.979
and I wanted to let you know

10:53.980 --> 10:56.682
that if I had to lose her,
I'm glad it was to you.

10:56.683 --> 10:58.567
Thank you.

10:58.568 --> 11:00.686
How did you get my address?

11:00.687 --> 11:02.254
Not important.

11:02.255 --> 11:04.189
Here, I brought you
a little gift.

11:04.190 --> 11:05.290
Okay.

11:05.291 --> 11:06.858
(chuckles)

11:06.859 --> 11:08.577
Nothing in here's
gonna bite me, is it?

11:08.578 --> 11:11.230
(chuckles)
Open it.

11:14.067 --> 11:15.134
Oh.

11:15.135 --> 11:16.368
Look at that.

11:16.369 --> 11:18.103
It's a picture of
Lyndsey and you.

11:18.104 --> 11:20.906
Yeah. Look how happy we were.

11:20.907 --> 11:22.641
We just found out
she was pregnant.

11:22.642 --> 11:25.060
It kind of looks like she's
glowing, but it's really just

11:25.061 --> 11:27.946
the lights from the Ferris wheel
on the Santa Monica Pier.

11:27.947 --> 11:30.249
I-I can't accept this.

11:30.250 --> 11:32.084
Oh, I want you to have it.

11:32.085 --> 11:34.219
You need to see
how happy Lyndsey made me,

11:34.220 --> 11:36.021
so you can be that happy.

11:36.022 --> 11:38.524
Okay, I'm not quite sure
I follow the logic,

11:38.525 --> 11:40.275
um, but-but thank you.

11:40.276 --> 11:41.293
See you around.

11:41.294 --> 11:42.294
(clicks tongue)

11:42.295 --> 11:43.729
(clicks tongue)

11:43.730 --> 11:44.997
Ah, it's too late, Alan.

11:44.998 --> 11:47.065
You're already dead.

11:58.711 --> 12:00.546
Well, that was a bit disturbing.

12:00.547 --> 12:02.114
♪ Men. ♪

12:03.448 --> 12:04.748
♪ Men. ♪

12:04.749 --> 12:08.914
Okay, uh, one decaf
grande soy chai latte

12:09.014 --> 12:10.465
with extra whipped cream.

12:10.466 --> 12:13.301
Uh, and a black
coffee for the lady.

12:13.302 --> 12:14.536
Thank you.

12:14.537 --> 12:16.087
I don't know how you
drink that stuff.

12:16.088 --> 12:17.455
Back at you.

12:17.456 --> 12:19.307
Name?
Uh, Alan.

12:19.308 --> 12:21.709
So, what's so important
that you didn't want

12:21.710 --> 12:22.977
to talk about it
on the phone?

12:22.978 --> 12:24.312
Oh, it's not that
it's important,

12:24.313 --> 12:25.513
uh, it's just
that it's...

12:25.514 --> 12:26.915
Alan, if you
dragged me down here

12:26.916 --> 12:28.750
to break up with me,
I will murder you.

12:28.751 --> 12:31.102
Oh, no, nobody's
breaking up.

12:31.103 --> 12:33.221
But, uh, speaking
of murder,

12:33.222 --> 12:35.290
I saw your
ex-husband yesterday.

12:35.291 --> 12:37.525
I'm sorry, "speaking of murder"?

12:37.526 --> 12:39.394
Oh, oh, maybe I should
back up a little.

12:39.395 --> 12:43.031
Um, Chris showed up at
my house and handed me

12:43.032 --> 12:46.634
what I consider to be a very
inappropriate photo of you two.

12:46.635 --> 12:48.269
That bastard!

12:48.270 --> 12:50.505
He told me he threw
those pictures away.

12:50.506 --> 12:53.774
Okay, I-I don't think we're
talking about the same pictures.

12:53.775 --> 12:57.412
Uh, but the point is, before
he left, he shot at me.

12:57.413 --> 12:59.214
He shot at you?

12:59.215 --> 13:00.882
Oh, not with a gun,
with his finger.

13:00.883 --> 13:02.917
But the implication
was pretty darn clear.

13:02.918 --> 13:05.153
Okay, let me
get this straight.

13:05.154 --> 13:07.055
I wasn't naked
in the picture?

13:07.056 --> 13:09.357
No, you were at the
Santa Monica Pier.

13:09.358 --> 13:12.293
But not naked, right?

13:12.294 --> 13:13.895
Right.

13:13.896 --> 13:15.513
Uh, but again,
my concern here

13:15.514 --> 13:18.166
is that your ex-husband
seems to be threatening me.

13:18.167 --> 13:19.868
Oh, Chris is harmless.

13:19.869 --> 13:22.036
His bark is way worse
than his bite.

13:22.037 --> 13:23.805
So you're saying
he does bite?

13:23.806 --> 13:25.306
Alan, you have nothing
to worry about.

13:25.307 --> 13:26.808
And if it'll make you
feel better,

13:26.809 --> 13:28.776
I'll talk to Chris
next time I see him.

13:28.777 --> 13:30.828
Talk to me about what?
What the hell?!

13:33.482 --> 13:35.516
How long have you
been sitting there?

13:35.517 --> 13:36.517
I just got here.

13:36.518 --> 13:37.685
I was gonna come say hi,

13:37.686 --> 13:39.120
but I thought
it was a little creepy--

13:39.121 --> 13:41.189
ex-husband, new boyfriend.

13:41.190 --> 13:42.390
Are you following us?

13:42.391 --> 13:44.859
No. I just stopped in
to have a cup of coffee.

13:44.860 --> 13:46.594
You live on
the other side of town.

13:46.595 --> 13:48.229
But I like the coffee here.

13:48.230 --> 13:51.799
Okay, I don't know what
you're trying to accomplish,

13:51.800 --> 13:53.268
but it needs to stop right now.

13:53.269 --> 13:56.003
Uh, I've got
this, Lyndsey.

13:56.004 --> 14:00.391
Now... listen up, pal.

14:00.392 --> 14:02.510
I'm dating your ex-wife,

14:02.511 --> 14:05.230
and there's nothing
you can do about it.

14:05.231 --> 14:06.281
Do you understand me?

14:06.282 --> 14:07.699
(shrieks):
Police! Police!

14:07.700 --> 14:08.683
Whoa.

14:08.684 --> 14:09.851
Calm down.

14:09.852 --> 14:11.786
Chris, get
out of here.

14:11.787 --> 14:13.738
I'm leaving.

14:13.739 --> 14:15.290
Oh, Alan.

14:15.291 --> 14:16.291
What?

14:16.292 --> 14:18.059
See you around.

14:18.060 --> 14:19.394
See? See?

14:19.395 --> 14:20.361
He shot me again!

14:20.362 --> 14:21.546
Calm down.

14:21.547 --> 14:22.997
Calm down?!
This guy is crazy.

14:22.998 --> 14:24.699
We need get a restraining order
or something.

14:24.700 --> 14:26.367
I don't think
that's necessary.

14:26.368 --> 14:28.052
Of course it's necessary.

14:28.053 --> 14:30.705
This is unacceptable behavior,
and I am not putting up with it.

14:30.706 --> 14:32.140
In fact,
forget the restraining order.

14:32.141 --> 14:34.259
I'm gonna pay him a visit
and make it crystal clear

14:34.260 --> 14:35.843
that he is messing with
the wrong guy.

14:35.844 --> 14:36.811
Alan!

14:36.812 --> 14:39.047
(shrieks):
Police! Police!

14:40.516 --> 14:42.383
♪ Men. ♪

14:42.384 --> 14:45.320
Oh, boy, oh, boy, oh, boy.

14:45.321 --> 14:46.721
Breakfast time.

14:46.722 --> 14:48.022
Esmerelda's huevos rancher...

14:48.023 --> 14:49.991
Oh, Berta!

14:49.992 --> 14:51.326
Hey.

14:51.327 --> 14:53.561
I thought you were
at a family reunion.

14:53.562 --> 14:54.595
Came home early.

14:54.596 --> 14:56.431
Turns out,
I don't like my family.

14:56.432 --> 14:58.833
So you came back.

14:58.834 --> 15:00.418
Yay.

15:00.419 --> 15:03.371
So Esmerelda's not
coming in anymore?

15:03.372 --> 15:04.939
No, I called her.

15:04.940 --> 15:06.907
She didn't mess things up
too bad, did she?

15:06.908 --> 15:08.459
No, no, no.
I mean, she's not you,

15:08.460 --> 15:10.678
so there was
a little adjustment.

15:12.581 --> 15:13.815
What's that
you're eating?

15:13.816 --> 15:15.099
Western omelette.

15:15.100 --> 15:16.684
Oh. Looks good.

15:16.685 --> 15:17.819
It is.

15:17.820 --> 15:19.954
Which reminds me,
you're out of eggs.

15:19.955 --> 15:21.422
(door opens, closes)

15:21.423 --> 15:22.457
ALAN:
Charlie?

15:22.458 --> 15:23.591
In here.

15:23.592 --> 15:25.393
Staring at me while I eat

15:25.394 --> 15:27.829
is making me
very uncomfortable.

15:27.830 --> 15:30.431
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

15:30.432 --> 15:31.649
Charlie, I've got
a problem.

15:31.650 --> 15:32.667
How about that,

15:32.668 --> 15:34.469
the problem's got a problem.

15:34.470 --> 15:36.120
Berta's back.

15:36.121 --> 15:37.905
Yay.

15:37.906 --> 15:40.708
I'm going somewhere
I can eat in peace.

15:40.709 --> 15:42.877
I thought my family
was annoying.

15:42.878 --> 15:45.046
Can you believe it?

15:45.047 --> 15:46.130
Esmerelda's gone.

15:46.131 --> 15:47.315
Yeah, boo-hoo.

15:47.316 --> 15:48.966
Lyndsey's ex-husband
threatened to kill me.

15:48.967 --> 15:50.084
How is that a bigger problem

15:50.085 --> 15:51.786
than me having to make
my own breakfast?

15:51.787 --> 15:53.137
I'm serious, Charlie.

15:53.138 --> 15:54.088
He's crazy.

15:54.089 --> 15:55.356
Well, of course
he's crazy.

15:55.357 --> 15:56.290
He's an ex-husband.

15:56.291 --> 15:57.325
The two words
go together.

15:57.326 --> 15:58.393
"Crazy ex-husband."

15:58.394 --> 15:59.327
I'm an ex-husband.

15:59.328 --> 16:00.595
There you go.

16:00.596 --> 16:02.263
Now, what are we gonna
do about Esmerelda?

16:02.264 --> 16:04.131
I mean, it's not like
I can fire Berta.

16:04.132 --> 16:06.801
Sure you can. Frankly,
I never cared for the woman.

16:06.802 --> 16:08.186
What am I gonna do
about Chris?

16:08.187 --> 16:09.937
I don't want to lose Lyndsey;
I love her.

16:09.938 --> 16:11.472
And I love
huevos rancheros

16:11.473 --> 16:14.158
and chocolate "felicidadas"
on my pillow.

16:14.159 --> 16:16.994
Okay, we seem to be talking
at cross purposes here.

16:16.995 --> 16:19.480
'Cause you're not focusing
on the real issue.

16:19.481 --> 16:21.816
I've just lost the best
housekeeper since...

16:21.817 --> 16:23.618
Wilma Flintstone.

16:24.670 --> 16:25.670
(screams)

16:25.671 --> 16:27.004
What the hell?

16:27.005 --> 16:28.489
What was that?

16:28.490 --> 16:30.324
A rock.

16:30.325 --> 16:32.009
It's got to be Chris.

16:32.010 --> 16:33.044
How can you be sure?

16:33.045 --> 16:34.762
Who else would
throw a rock at me?

16:34.763 --> 16:37.465
Good point. I'm here
and Mom's out of town.

16:37.466 --> 16:39.634
I ain't cleaning that up.

16:42.638 --> 16:44.672
♪ Men. ♪

16:44.673 --> 16:46.023
(TV playing quietly)

16:46.024 --> 16:48.943
(phone rings)

16:48.944 --> 16:50.144
Hello.

16:51.947 --> 16:53.147
Hello?

16:54.083 --> 16:57.351
("Up, Up and Away"
ringtone playing)

17:01.523 --> 17:03.224
Hello?

17:03.225 --> 17:05.226
Hello?!

17:05.227 --> 17:07.428
Okay, whoever this is,

17:07.429 --> 17:09.196
you should know
that you're not scaring me.

17:09.197 --> 17:11.065
(doorbell rings, Alan screams)

17:17.206 --> 17:18.256
Esmerelda!

17:18.257 --> 17:19.707
Come on in.

17:19.708 --> 17:21.426
&lt;i>Buenas noches, Señor Harper.&lt;/i>

17:26.648 --> 17:28.516
Yeah, yeah, me, too.

17:29.751 --> 17:30.735
Esmerelda?

17:30.736 --> 17:33.554
&lt;i>Oh, como esta, Señor Alan?&lt;/i>

17:33.555 --> 17:34.906
&lt;i>Muy bien.&lt;/i>

17:34.907 --> 17:36.023
Charlie, what's going on?

17:36.024 --> 17:37.224
&lt;i>Excusez-moi.&lt;/i>

17:39.261 --> 17:42.563
From now on, Berta will be
our day housekeeper

17:42.564 --> 17:44.866
and Esmerelda will be
our night housekeeper.

17:44.867 --> 17:46.134
&lt;i>Capiche?&lt;/i>

17:46.135 --> 17:47.502
Does Berta know?

17:47.503 --> 17:48.936
Berta doesn't need to know.

17:48.937 --> 17:51.105
Uh-huh. So what's she gonna
think when she comes back

17:51.106 --> 17:53.591
and she sees the pointed toilet
paper and the swan towels?

17:53.592 --> 17:54.709
Way ahead of you.

17:54.710 --> 17:56.711
I'll just un-swan
and un-point everything

17:56.712 --> 17:57.812
before she gets here.

17:57.813 --> 17:59.430
Then why do it?

17:59.431 --> 18:01.048
I mean, is it
worth the trouble

18:01.049 --> 18:02.550
to sneak around
behind Berta's back?

18:02.551 --> 18:04.919
I know it's crazy, but...

18:06.755 --> 18:08.589
...the woman makes me happy.

18:09.758 --> 18:11.476
&lt;i>Botanas, Señor Harper?&lt;/i>

18:11.477 --> 18:14.111
&lt;i>Oh, si... vous&lt;/i> plaît.

18:16.865 --> 18:18.483
How about that?

18:18.484 --> 18:20.301
I'm even starting
to pick up the language.

18:20.302 --> 18:22.136
It's a shame the
language is French.

18:22.137 --> 18:23.137
(phone rings)

18:23.138 --> 18:25.072
(screams)

18:25.073 --> 18:27.241
♪ Men. ♪

18:28.563 --> 18:30.797
♪ Men. ♪

18:34.924 --> 18:37.026
Alan, relax.
If Chris wanted to kill you,

18:37.027 --> 18:38.894
he'd just climb through your
window while you're sleeping

18:38.895 --> 18:41.597
and smother you
with a pillow.

18:41.598 --> 18:43.299
Thank you,
that's very helpful.

18:43.300 --> 18:45.985
At least, that's how
I always imagined doing it.

18:45.986 --> 18:47.670
BERTA:
You rat bastard.

18:48.772 --> 18:51.206
Berta!

18:51.207 --> 18:52.641
It's not what it looks like.

18:52.642 --> 18:53.709
Is that so?

18:53.710 --> 18:55.377
Then what is it?

18:55.378 --> 18:59.465
Uh... it's purely sexual.

19:01.051 --> 19:02.651
I'm not stupid, Charlie.

19:02.652 --> 19:04.336
I know when I'm being two-timed.

19:04.337 --> 19:05.571
Charlie, I'm shocked.

19:05.572 --> 19:06.605
Shocked!

19:06.606 --> 19:09.091
Berta, I-I had no idea
this was going...

19:09.092 --> 19:10.059
Stay out of it, Zippy!

19:10.060 --> 19:12.594
I'm out.

19:12.595 --> 19:14.330
So what do you have to say
for yourself?

19:14.331 --> 19:15.731
Berta, I am... I am so sorry.

19:15.732 --> 19:18.167
I got carried away, but I think
if we all sit down like adults

19:18.168 --> 19:19.835
and talk this through,
we can make it work.

19:19.836 --> 19:20.936
Uh-uh.

19:20.937 --> 19:22.304
It's either me or her.

19:22.305 --> 19:23.872
Oh, please don't make me choose.

19:23.873 --> 19:25.441
Berta, I love you both.

19:25.442 --> 19:26.575
Good-bye, Charlie.

19:26.576 --> 19:27.643
No, wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait, wait.

19:34.617 --> 19:36.552
It's you, Berta.

19:36.553 --> 19:38.087
It's always been you.

19:38.088 --> 19:40.255
I'm sorry.

19:40.256 --> 19:42.207
It's just not our time.

19:43.827 --> 19:46.128
Please tell her how sorry I am.

19:46.129 --> 19:48.330
(speaking Spanish)

19:57.691 --> 19:59.674
(both laugh)

20:02.345 --> 20:05.114
&lt;i>Adios, Señor Harper.&lt;/i>

20:05.115 --> 20:08.016
Arrivederci, Esmerelda.

20:09.486 --> 20:10.753
Okay, then.

20:10.754 --> 20:11.987
I'll see you tomorrow.

20:11.988 --> 20:13.455
Good, good.

20:13.456 --> 20:14.456
I'll be late.

20:14.457 --> 20:15.724
It's okay.

20:15.725 --> 20:17.760
You might want to clean
that hair up off the floor

20:17.761 --> 20:18.927
before I get in.

20:18.928 --> 20:21.380
Sure, I'm on it.
Okay.

20:24.551 --> 20:26.735
(sighs)

20:28.772 --> 20:30.973
Oh, Esmerelda.

20:33.343 --> 20:35.444
No.

20:35.445 --> 20:37.379
No, I can't let her go.

20:41.351 --> 20:42.751
Oh, hey, Chris.

20:42.752 --> 20:45.437
Pillows on the couch, Alan's
in his room. Esmerelda!

20:45.438 --> 20:48.923
== Sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00ff00">elderman&lt;/font> ==
